# Generated by the ladder scripts; every one regenerates from a script
# beside it. gen_*_harness.py writes the harness and stub sources, the
# bundle scripts write *-subject.codex, the cycles write the rest.
*.ir
*.ir.map
*.truth
# ...except a bank. A working truth beside the rung regenerates by rerunning
# the rung, so it stays out; a bank under truth/<update>/ is the measurement
# itself, taken deliberately by bank_truth.py, and is the only artifact that
# can say what an Update changed in the emitted image.
!truth/**/*.truth
*.zig
*.zigout
*.diff
*.blob
*.cdx
*.cdx.map
*-subject.codex
# The built zigc and the fingerprint that says what built it. Both are
# artifacts of zigc_verify.sh and both regenerate from it; the .fp is what
# lets a rerun skip the expensive half, and a stale one in git would be a
# claim about a tree it was never built in.
/zigc
/zigc.fp
__pycache__/
recon/
ringplug-source.codex
*.cce
*.cce.map
*.blob.stage1
*.transport.log
# Written by ring_compile.py: the full diagnostic list for a compile.
# Regenerates with the rung, so it stays out of the tree; the point is
# that it exists at all, not that it is versioned.
*.diags
.zig-cache/
# Hand-written, not emitted: the *.zig rule above is about plug output, and
# this is the program that runs it.
!ast/f3_run.zig

# Harnesses and stubs are written by the gen_*_harness.py beside them, and
# truth_arm regenerates before every bundle. A committed copy is a second
# authority that can disagree with its generator, and 90k lines of it made
# the branch unreviewable.
ast/*Harness.codex
ast/*Stubs.codex
# ...except the ones nothing generates. MinHarness is hand-written, and these
# two stubs stand in for chapters a subset build cannot carry (see
# BootPaintStubs.codex for why the real painter cannot come along).
!ast/MinHarness.codex
!ast/BootPaintStubs.codex
!ast/LexStubs.codex

# native_build.sh output; regenerates from the sources beside it.
native/

# Editor swap files: a session leaves these behind and one got committed.
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Run intermediates: one unit answers for several rungs, so the raw stream
# lands here before split_truth cuts it up.
*.raw
*.stdout
*.zigraw

# Nightly console logs; tonight.sh rewrites them every run.
logs/*
!logs/.gitignore
ast/ringplug.cdx.fp
ringplug-source-check.codex
# EVERY provenance sidecar, not just a truth's. `*.truth.prov` was the rule
# for a long time, which left `ast/<unit>.ir.prov` TRACKED -- twelve files that
# every truth arm rewrites (`truth_prov.py stamp-ir`), so a checkout that had
# run anything was permanently dirty and `sandbox.sh`'s own header claiming
# "*.prov is gitignored" was half true. Read 2026-09-02: the committed copies
# are never consulted. `check_ir` refuses on a missing `ast/<unit>.ir` BEFORE
# it opens the sidecar, `.ir` is ignored so a fresh sandbox never has one, and
# any run that does produce the IR rewrites the sidecar in the same step. Not
# a pin -- files tracked before the ignore rules caught up.
*.prov
# ...except a banked one, for the same reason its truth is kept. The sidecar
# is the measurement's own record of what produced it -- the seed, and the
# harness content -- and a bank without it is a set of numbers nobody can
# place afterwards. Keeping it is also what lets restore_truths.py put a
# bank back into a fresh sandbox instead of re-measuring for half an hour:
# the arms then check a sidecar that travelled with its truth, rather than
# one somebody reconstructed.
!truth/**/*.truth.prov
.agentgrid
!logs/INDEX.md
findings/.tier-run/
ast/.stack-probe/
*.self.zig
# The corpus census keeps ONE tracked artifact: corpus/census.json, the bank,
# written only by --bank. Everything else in corpus/ is a derived stage output
# that every run rewrites, and tracking those is what broke the census on
# 2026-08-27.
#
# transpile.json, gaps.json and run.json/run.jsonl were tracked AND rewritten
# by every run, so the discipline became "revert them afterwards"
# (overnight_verify.sh did exactly that with a `git checkout --`). The tracked
# copies then froze at whenever someone last committed them on purpose while
# census.json advanced through --bank, and the two disagreed: a stale
# transpile.json held 596 programs and no `zigemit` bucket where census.json
# held 606 and had one, and a stale run.jsonl called programs `refused` that
# census.json called `match` and that build clean today. A resume read the
# stale one and reported 94 phantom regressions.
#
# A bank is taken deliberately. A stage output is regenerated. Do not track a
# file that every run rewrites.
/corpus/transpile.json
/corpus/gaps.json
/corpus/run.json
/corpus/run.jsonl
ast/ringplug-compile.log
